(438431, 40375, 11506, '<td valign="top">Good Irony, but I would have like this shot better with a little better setup.  I think you could have captured this on a white or black backgound.  (paper or sheet) The towel''s design detracts from the subject(s) here.</td>', 'Good Irony, but I would have like this shot better with a little better setup.  I think you could have captured this on a white or black backgound.  (paper or sheet) The towel''s design detracts from the subject(s) here.', '2003-10-02 18:59:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(438433, 40169, 11506, '<td valign="top">A little bit too much glare just below the dish.  The shot is a little off center and rotated a few degrees.  I think to pull something like this off, it has to be dead center and straight.</td>', 'A little bit too much glare just below the dish.  The shot is a little off center and rotated a few degrees.  I think to pull something like this off, it has to be dead center and straight.', '2003-10-02 19:01:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(438435, 40233, 11506, '<td valign="top">This is a good capture and strikes emotion into the viewer.  I can''t help but feel sorry for it.  I love how it''s looking at the camera.  I''m usually ont a big fan of borders but I like this one here.  I''m wondering if a red (same color as the bird) neatline would add anything to this?</td>', 'This is a good capture and strikes emotion into the viewer.  I can''t help but feel sorry for it.  I love how it''s looking at the camera.  I''m usually ont a big fan of borders but I like this one here.  I''m wondering if a red (same color as the bird) neatline would add anything to this?', '2003-10-02 19:04:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(438436, 40054, 11506, '<td valign="top">Ok, I have to defend this as a Transportation Planner :)  Oh, nevermind.  I do like the desaturation here.  It really brings out the sign.</td>', 'Ok, I have to defend this as a Transportation Planner :)  Oh, nevermind.  I do like the desaturation here.  It really brings out the sign.', '2003-10-02 19:07:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(438438, 39955, 7778, '<td valign="top">Given the sheer bulk of irrelevant and horrific entries to this demanding challenge, I''m awarding extra points to this fitting image. The irony (and a fine one!), IMO, is more contextual than purely interpretative, which does make for an unusual artistic licence.<br/> <br/>The photo itself (IMO) would not be able to stand on its own legs outside and beyond the confines of the challenge, both technically and aesthetically. Whatever the particular shortcomings (the extreme soft focus, a near-centred assymetry ((of composition)), actually serve a sense of irony. The idea, however, remains more dominant than the photo itself.<br/> <br/>The simple, straightforward title awards a rare sincerity to this entry, which would make a highly unusual attribute to ironic intent.<br/> <br/>I wish this image will not get entirely lost in the sea of cretins! <br/> <br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Given the sheer bulk of irrelevant and horrific entries to this demanding challenge, I''m awarding extra points to this fitting image. The irony (and a fine one!), IMO, is more contextual than purely interpretative, which does make for an unusual artistic licence. The photo itself (IMO) would not be able to stand on its own legs outside and beyond the confines of the challenge, both technically and aesthetically. Whatever the particular shortcomings (the extreme soft focus, a near-centred assymetry ((of composition)), actually serve a sense of irony. The idea, however, remains more dominant than the photo itself. The simple, straightforward title awards a rare sincerity to this entry, which would make a highly unusual attribute to ironic intent. I wish this image will not get entirely lost in the sea of cretins!    ', '2003-10-02 19:10:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(438439, 39953, 11506, '<td valign="top">Wow.  This is facinating.  I''m finding myself saying- you''re right, this IS kind of beautiful in it''s own way.  Maybe this is why people stare at accidents???  Good job thinking outside the box.  8</td>', 'Wow.  This is facinating.  I''m finding myself saying- you''re right, this IS kind of beautiful in it''s own way.  Maybe this is why people stare at accidents???  Good job thinking outside the box.  8', '2003-10-02 19:11:45.000000', NULL, 1),
