(442016, 40362, 327, '<td valign="top">Enjoyed this shot! Funny and done well. Congrats.</td>', 'Enjoyed this shot! Funny and done well. Congrats.', '2003-10-08 01:11:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(442018, 40123, 12425, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all your comments.<br/>The ''stars'' were added using an ''in-camera'' digital filter, "white cross filter".  The camera decides where to put the stars, based on bright highlights.  <br/>Once the pic was out of the camera, main adjustments were saturation, where I removed all colors except blue and magenta, and increased the hue of blue to make the purple more vibrant.<br/>Oh, and for those who didnt see the irony - you mustnt know many Catholic girls :)<br/>(PS - 24 1''s and 2''s?  Come on, it wasnt THAT bad.  Maybe you all thought it was spot-edited?  Ah well.)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-10-08 00:16:51.</i></td>', 'Thanks for all your comments.The ''stars'' were added using an ''in-camera'' digital filter, "white cross filter".  The camera decides where to put the stars, based on bright highlights.  Once the pic was out of the camera, main adjustments were saturation, where I removed all colors except blue and magenta, and increased the hue of blue to make the purple more vibrant.Oh, and for those who didnt see the irony - you mustnt know many Catholic girls :)(PS - 24 1''s and 2''s?  Come on, it wasnt THAT bad.  Maybe you all thought it was spot-edited?  Ah well.)', '2003-10-08 01:12:35.000000', '2003-10-08 01:16:51.000000', 0),
(442032, 39648, 10125, '<td valign="top">Ok....this is at the exit/entrance of a divided highway (Rt72@Rt177) in Plainville Connecticut. I croped out the road to hide the fact that the no left turn sign was to prevent people from going up the exit ramp. The left turn only lane starts after this. Where I took this shot there is only one lane. Having driven many years, I find it is rough on the sheet metal of the drivers door to turn left from a right lane. The picture wouldn''t have been as funny showing the road. Thank you all for your comments....Steve</td>', 'Ok....this is at the exit/entrance of a divided highway (Rt72@Rt177) in Plainville Connecticut. I croped out the road to hide the fact that the no left turn sign was to prevent people from going up the exit ramp. The left turn only lane starts after this. Where I took this shot there is only one lane. Having driven many years, I find it is rough on the sheet metal of the drivers door to turn left from a right lane. The picture wouldn''t have been as funny showing the road. Thank you all for your comments....Steve', '2003-10-08 01:18:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(442039, 39921, 11895, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments.  Irony was a difficult theme for me.  Hope my comments above make my entry clearer.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments.  Irony was a difficult theme for me.  Hope my comments above make my entry clearer.', '2003-10-08 01:23:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(442072, 40362, 5705, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all of you you took the time to comment.<br/>39 Comments!  and most were positive.<br/> <br/>I thought of this idea late, and on Tuesday after work I thought I try it out--<br/> <br/>Like I said, there was NO LIGHT,, so I bumped the ISO to 200, and wasnt sure how it was gonna turn out (200 ISO on some digi-cams can be real noisy)-- but it cam out clean enuf and didnt have any "shake" warning--<br/> <br/>The dead hunter is my mom, she was really into the idea and we alot of fun-- <br/> <br/>I know its a low scoring challenge, but thanks for all the comments and votes--<br/> <br/>Now look out, Im going for blue next!!<br/> <br/> <br/>Here are some outakes from the shoot--<br/> <br/><a href="//gallery.powershot-a.com/album34" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//gallery.powershot-a.com/album34</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-10-08 00:54:28.</i></td>', 'Thanks for all of you you took the time to comment.39 Comments!  and most were positive. I thought of this idea late, and on Tuesday after work I thought I try it out-- Like I said, there was NO LIGHT,, so I bumped the ISO to 200, and wasnt sure how it was gonna turn out (200 ISO on some digi-cams can be real noisy)-- but it cam out clean enuf and didnt have any "shake" warning-- The dead hunter is my mom, she was really into the idea and we alot of fun--  I know its a low scoring challenge, but thanks for all the comments and votes-- Now look out, Im going for blue next!!  Here are some outakes from the shoot-- //gallery.powershot-a.com/album34', '2003-10-08 01:50:38.000000', '2003-10-08 01:54:28.000000', 0),
