(442703, 39919, 11487, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all your comments.  This is very encouraging to me.</td>', 'Thanks for all your comments.  This is very encouraging to me.', '2003-10-08 09:52:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(442708, 40361, 5728, '<td valign="top">Ah Sher I should have guessed this is yours. It was my top favourite and I was sure it would be in the top 3, so it''s a little dissapointing to find it back here, and even more disappointing to see so many 1''s, 2''s and 3''s.</td>', 'Ah Sher I should have guessed this is yours. It was my top favourite and I was sure it would be in the top 3, so it''s a little dissapointing to find it back here, and even more disappointing to see so many 1''s, 2''s and 3''s.', '2003-10-08 09:54:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(442856, 39539, 12061, '<td valign="top">I would''ve voted 0 but it doesn''t exist.</td>', 'I would''ve voted 0 but it doesn''t exist.', '2003-10-08 11:00:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(442980, 40168, 6845, '<td valign="top">I would like to thank every one for their comments. I would really like to thank those who gave me a chance to explain my image.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-10-08 17:27:25.</i></td>', 'I would like to thank every one for their comments. I would really like to thank those who gave me a chance to explain my image.', '2003-10-08 11:54:34.000000', '2003-10-08 18:27:25.000000', 0),
(443151, 40232, 6870, '<td valign="top">Thanks all. I really wanted the DO NOT ENTER sign to be larger and out of focus--and perhaps only a corner of it visible, and the River Heights Welcomes You sign to be more distant. This would have added some drama and interest, though it would have been more subtle--especially for international folks who don''t know what a DO NOT ENTER sign in the U.S. looks like. But the signs were too close to each other, and I could not get a radical depth of field because of other various obstacles that you can''t see: a river, a pole, some trees, etc. But I was pleased that I was able to communicate the irony anyway. Thanks again.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-10-08 15:34:49.</i></td>', 'Thanks all. I really wanted the DO NOT ENTER sign to be larger and out of focus--and perhaps only a corner of it visible, and the River Heights Welcomes You sign to be more distant. This would have added some drama and interest, though it would have been more subtle--especially for international folks who don''t know what a DO NOT ENTER sign in the U.S. looks like. But the signs were too close to each other, and I could not get a radical depth of field because of other various obstacles that you can''t see: a river, a pole, some trees, etc. But I was pleased that I was able to communicate the irony anyway. Thanks again.', '2003-10-08 12:51:41.000000', '2003-10-08 16:34:49.000000', 0),
(443280, 40362, 11153, '<td valign="top">Sorry, but i don´t like dead animals, speacially using them as a trophy. I hate this one.</td>', 'Sorry, but i don´t like dead animals, speacially using them as a trophy. I hate this one.', '2003-10-08 13:46:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(443328, 40362, 11206, '<td valign="top">This was one of the BEST!!!  I thought so anyway.  Congrats on the ribbon. It was well deserved.  I Love this so much, I''m making it one of my favorites.  I love Hunting and this goes to show you what would happen if it was flipped.  Thanks.</td>', 'This was one of the BEST!!!  I thought so anyway.  Congrats on the ribbon. It was well deserved.  I Love this so much, I''m making it one of my favorites.  I love Hunting and this goes to show you what would happen if it was flipped.  Thanks.', '2003-10-08 14:13:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(443334, 40232, 11206, '<td valign="top">I should of figured this was you.  Great job.  This was one of my favorites along with the deer picture.  Congrats on the ribbon.</td>', 'I should of figured this was you.  Great job.  This was one of my favorites along with the deer picture.  Congrats on the ribbon.', '2003-10-08 14:18:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(443345, 40362, 255, '<td valign="top">too funny! <br/>congrats on yet another ribbon buzz! :)</td>', 'too funny! congrats on yet another ribbon buzz! :)', '2003-10-08 14:22:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(443374, 39533, 12268, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kiwiness:</b></div><hr/><i>Looks like a photo of Matt Damon, am I right? So how did you get the rainbow? A prism?</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>dunno really. I was on the compuer &amp; I looked up &amp; there it was. Some type of reflection from my window.<br/> <br/>Yeah, no, it''s not Matt Damon. Just some random postacrd at the Yaffa Cafe that I picked up<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-10-08 13:43:12.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by kiwiness:Looks like a photo of Matt Damon, am I right? So how did you get the rainbow? A prism?  dunno really. I was on the compuer & I looked up & there it was. Some type of reflection from my window. Yeah, no, it''s not Matt Damon. Just some random postacrd at the Yaffa Cafe that I picked up', '2003-10-08 14:42:06.000000', '2003-10-08 14:43:12.000000', 0),
(443377, 39533, 12268, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by oskar:</b></div><hr/><i>hmmmmm spotedit ???</i></td></tr></table> <br/>what''s that?</td>', 'Originally posted by oskar:hmmmmm spotedit ??? what''s that?', '2003-10-08 14:43:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(443378, 39533, 12268, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hgpayne:</b></div><hr/><i>base 1: 1/1; challenge: 0/3; technical: 2/3; aesthetics: 1/3; total: 4</i></td></tr></table> <br/>interesting breakdown of scoring. What does base stand represent?</td>', 'Originally posted by hgpayne:base 1: 1/1; challenge: 0/3; technical: 2/3; aesthetics: 1/3; total: 4 interesting breakdown of scoring. What does base stand represent?', '2003-10-08 14:45:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(443399, 40232, 5728, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by dsidwell:</b></div><hr/><i>This would have added some drama and interest, though it would have been more subtle--especially for international folks who don''t know what a DO NOT ENTER sign in the U.S. looks like.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Nice of you to think of us international folks too David :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by dsidwell:This would have added some drama and interest, though it would have been more subtle--especially for international folks who don''t know what a DO NOT ENTER sign in the U.S. looks like.  Nice of you to think of us international folks too David :-)', '2003-10-08 15:01:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(443418, 40232, 9411, '<td valign="top">Congrat''s... Glad to see you back in the winners circle.</td>', 'Congrat''s... Glad to see you back in the winners circle.', '2003-10-08 15:11:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(443444, 40028, 5705, '<td valign="top">Shoulda scored way better--<br/> <br/></td>', 'Shoulda scored way better-- ', '2003-10-08 15:25:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(443702, 40319, 4015, '<td valign="top">Thank you all very much for all the comments and the votes on my entry. I am an amateur and thanks to this site and the people on it, I am learning more everyday.  This is a wonderful site and I am honored to have placed at all when there are so many wonderful photographers on this site. Everyone that comments on any photo helps the photographer in one way or another, whether it is an in depth comment on how to improve the photo or just a word of encouragement.<br/>Again, thank you all very much.</td>', 'Thank you all very much for all the comments and the votes on my entry. I am an amateur and thanks to this site and the people on it, I am learning more everyday.  This is a wonderful site and I am honored to have placed at all when there are so many wonderful photographers on this site. Everyone that comments on any photo helps the photographer in one way or another, whether it is an in depth comment on how to improve the photo or just a word of encouragement.Again, thank you all very much.', '2003-10-08 17:18:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(443782, 40362, 6504, '<td valign="top">As for the person who doesn''t like the dead deer,  how do you know for sure it''s dead??  hahaha.<br/> <br/>I''m not a hunting fan either, and this picture expresses what I wish really would happen to hunters.</td>', 'As for the person who doesn''t like the dead deer,  how do you know for sure it''s dead??  hahaha. I''m not a hunting fan either, and this picture expresses what I wish really would happen to hunters.', '2003-10-08 17:53:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(443803, 39865, 12462, '<td valign="top">Thanks a lot for you comments everybody. Actually I kept the right side intentionally, to show the surroundings and give a flavor of the moment...anyway. Thanx again.</td>', 'Thanks a lot for you comments everybody. Actually I kept the right side intentionally, to show the surroundings and give a flavor of the moment...anyway. Thanx again.', '2003-10-08 18:08:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(443832, 40217, 5313, '<td valign="top">What a great photo, Doug!  Love it!</td>', 'What a great photo, Doug!  Love it!', '2003-10-08 18:27:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(444061, 39539, 9907, '<td valign="top">First of all thank you to everyone who felt compeled to comment.<br/>I knew they would range from disgust to wow, but when I saw the cat there was more than just a dead cat.  And unlike some who feel this is not art I beg to differ, if all you see is a dead cat your not looking.<br/>The composition of the image tells the story...ie. the double yellow lines, the tire marks, the look of total fear on the face.<br/>The contrast was a problem there is a small area where cat and street tend to come together but when I printed the look is much better.<br/>But thanks will do better with it next time, I hope the matter of well thought out photos continue and once agian thanks</td>', 'First of all thank you to everyone who felt compeled to comment.I knew they would range from disgust to wow, but when I saw the cat there was more than just a dead cat.  And unlike some who feel this is not art I beg to differ, if all you see is a dead cat your not looking.The composition of the image tells the story...ie. the double yellow lines, the tire marks, the look of total fear on the face.The contrast was a problem there is a small area where cat and street tend to come together but when I printed the look is much better.But thanks will do better with it next time, I hope the matter of well thought out photos continue and once agian thanks', '2003-10-08 20:43:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(444217, 40319, 9581, '<td valign="top">Ya know that is some good thinking! Great mind! I think you care and take the time to look at subject before you snap the picture! Even if its quick thinking before capturing. Go deep and look abstract finding things that might really not be there! You have  great talent.</td>', 'Ya know that is some good thinking! Great mind! I think you care and take the time to look at subject before you snap the picture! Even if its quick thinking before capturing. Go deep and look abstract finding things that might really not be there! You have  great talent.', '2003-10-08 22:27:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(444706, 39821, 9982, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kiwiness:</b></div><hr/><i>Could you explain this one perhaps. I looked at it a couple of times but honestly couldn''t find the irony in it.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The sign said Welcome to Finsbury Park (a notoriously grim area of London) but most of the lights inside are broken, its covered in grafitti, its raining, dark, cold and miserable.<br/> <br/>Plenty of people said they didn''t understand. It must be me.</td>', 'Originally posted by kiwiness:Could you explain this one perhaps. I looked at it a couple of times but honestly couldn''t find the irony in it.  The sign said Welcome to Finsbury Park (a notoriously grim area of London) but most of the lights inside are broken, its covered in grafitti, its raining, dark, cold and miserable. Plenty of people said they didn''t understand. It must be me.', '2003-10-09 06:02:35.000000', NULL, 0),
